## PHASE 2 — MODEL QUALITY & CORRECTNESS (Task 6 & Task 7)

This is the substantive analytical fix: two "high-ROC-AUC, useless-in-practice" classifiers and one
regression model that loses to the mean on real held-out data. Applies to both branches — the underlying
model code exists in both `task-mode`'s Task 6/7 practicals and `proj-mode`'s `app/intelligence/ml/` and
`app/intelligence/dl/`.

### Entries to close (from `TODO.md`)

1. **Pit-decision classifier (Task 6) is unusable at its operating point** (High) — test PR-AUC 0.25, F1
   0.077 despite ROC-AUC 0.98, because pit events are 4.8% of laps. In
   `app/intelligence/ml/classification.py`: add `class_weight="balanced"` to classifier configs; evaluate
   resampling (SMOTE or undersampling) **inside CV folds only** (never on the test set, never before the
   split — this is the same leakage discipline as Task 5). Tune the decision threshold on validation folds
   to maximise F1 or expected cost, persist the chosen threshold into `model_registry.json`. Make PR-AUC,
   not ROC-AUC, the primary selection metric in `app/intelligence/ml/selection.py`. Surface
   precision/recall/F1 next to ROC-AUC on `frontend/app/machine-learning/page.tsx`.
2. **Task 7's DNN pit classifier is degenerate at its operating point** (High) — F1/precision/recall
   exactly 0.0 at threshold 0.5; it predicts "never pit" for every test lap. Same fix pattern as #1, applied
   in `app/intelligence/dl/tuning.py`: tune the threshold on validation data, make PR-AUC the primary
   selection metric, surface precision/recall/F1 on the new `/deep-learning` page alongside `/machine-learning`.
3. **Selected regression model (Task 6) has negative test R²** (High) — `decision_tree` is selected on CV
